u} is taken to be a general complex 3 × 3 3	imes 3 matrix, its real and imaginary parts provide 18 real parameters. Together with the two heavy-mass ratios, the logarithmic scale parameter, and the two phases, the parameter vector has dimension d G = 23 d_{G}=23 . The observable vector contains two mass-squared differences and the nine absolute values of the PMNS matrix elements, and hence has dimension d L = 11 d_{L}=11 . The following ranges are adopted for each element of G G . − 1 ≤ { Re Y i ​ α ν , Im Y i ​ α ν } ≤ 1 , 10 − 5 ≤ { | M 1 | M 3 , | M 2 | M 3 } ≤ 1 , − π ≤ { arg ⁡ M 1 , arg ⁡ M 2 } ≤ π , − 1.22 ≤ log 10 ⁡ ( ⟨ H ⟩ 2 M 3 / meV ) ≤ 2.78 . \displaystyle egin{split}-1\leq\left\{eal Y_{i\alpha}^{
